"It was a dreadful night\nNot like something touched its might\nIt was still unshaken\nEven though it had mistaken\n\nThose mistakes rust iron\nA mountain is immune to it\nIt's so huge that even quakes\nCan barely move an inch of it\n\nIt's so majestic that blood stains\nThey look nothing but insignificant\nThe beauty and magnificence remains\nIt's so maestoso and diligent\n\nDiligent to the trees it has\nDiligent to the birds who nest\nDiligent to the beasts who rest\nDiligent to the bugs and pest\n\nIt's so unshaken it can't be tainted\nIt's so fullfilled it doesn't need a to beg\nIt's so it it shelters others\nIt's so it it cannot brag\n\nBe like the mountain which cannot be pushed\nBe like it you cannot be pulled\nBe like the peaks so they can't reach you\nBut be so humble a range will get you"